  "historical_output_text": " When my cat escaped through our slightly airtightly secured door for a short adventure in unfamiliar surroundings on a warm Saturday afternoon last summer while the rest stayed behind in our air-condition, it turned our mundane routine topsy, and we all had a bit extra for a while as my family, our furbaby companion.\n\nI noticed the kitchen was quiet when it was supposed to still brim in her playful, purric, and footpad sounds. Concern crept through. After checking our house for the fussy fur ball I had been missing, she wasn’t. The air was warm outside with the afternoon sunshine beating on it.\n\nWith my phone camera and an old tarp I had left on a window step just outside to keep stray cat from coming inside and making mischief with my plants. I ventured onto the patio with it hoping to spot some sign",
